# The checks of the C++ tests: the package's, less two. A test's numbers are
# the amounts, dates, and counts its claims name, so they are not magic; and a
# test reads an optional it expects present with value(), which ends the run
# when it is absent, rather than checking it first, as it reads the value of a
# call it expects the library to accept.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -readability-magic-numbers
